        ":question/problem": "Calculate $X+(Y-Z)$, where\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n| $X+(Y-Z)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X+(Y-Z) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}+(\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}9-2 & 8-3 \\\\ 3-1 & 7-4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4+7 & 6+5 \\\\ 2+2 & 5+3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
