        ":question/id": "27e624e6-a59a-5c4b-b6d9-58636961fd76",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-69636",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $R+S+T$, where\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,S=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -5 \\\\ 12 & -8 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,T=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R+S+T & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -5 \\\\ 12 & -8 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3+7+3 & -3+(-5)+0 \\\\ -4+12+0 & 2+(-8)+7 \\\\ -1+5+0 & -5+(-3)+2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -8 \\\\ 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      }
